<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 December, from 1118 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1118">1118 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">908 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfonso I of Aragon takes Zaragoza from the Almoravids</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a>, known as the Battler, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, the most important Almoravid city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and made it the capital of his kingdom. Its fall marked the deterioration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>' northern front.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1271">1271 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">755 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kublai Khan proclaims the Yuan dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, proclaimed the dynastic name Great Yuan for his realm in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The Yuan completed the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> in 1279 and ruled China until 1368.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1499">1499 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">527 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An uprising against forced conversions breaks out in Granada</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albaicin">Albaicín</a>, a crowd killed a constable taking a woman away for questioning after she cried out that she was being forced to become Christian. It began the Rebellion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpujarras">Alpujarras</a> against mass forced conversions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rebellion-of-the-alpujarras-1499-1501">Rebellion of the Alpujarras</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Americans observe the first national day of thanksgiving</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> set aside 18 December as a day of thanksgiving for the victory at Saratoga. It was the first such national observance by the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 13th Amendment abolishing slavery is proclaimed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State William Seward certified that the 13th Amendment had been ratified by the required number of states. It abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, freeing about four million people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'Piltdown Man' is presented to the Geological Society</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Dawson and Arthur Smith Woodward announced fossils from Piltdown in Sussex as an early human ancestor. In 1953 they were exposed as a forgery combining a human skull and an orang-utan jaw.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Verdun ends</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After ten months of fighting, French counter-attacks closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a>. About 700,000 French and German soldiers were killed, wounded or missing, and the front was almost back where it began.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1958">1958 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US launches SCORE, the first communications satellite</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> rocket placed Project SCORE in orbit. The next day it broadcast a recorded Christmas message from President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a>, the first voice transmitted from space.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-yoshitaka"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouchi-yoshitaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ōuchi Yoshitaka</span><span class="tp">1507–1551</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria</span><span class="tp">1863–1914</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-burton-harrison"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-burton-harrison.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Burton Harrison</span><span class="tp">1873–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-stalin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Stalin</span><span class="tp">1878–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/steve-biko"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/steve-biko.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Steve Biko</span><span class="tp">1946–1977</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lawrence-wong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lawrence-wong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lawrence Wong</span><span class="tp">b. 1972</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 December <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottfried-herder"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-gottfried-herder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Gottfried Herder</span><span class="tp">1744–1803</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vaclav-havel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vaclav-havel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Václav Havel</span><span class="tp">1936–2011</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
